{"name":"Scarecrow Frown","hex":"#a55e2b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scarecrow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An effigy, typically made of straw and dressed in old clothes, fixed to a pole in a field to deter birds from eating crops or seeds planted there. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person or animal regarded as resembling a scarecrow (sense 1) in some way; especially, a tall, thin, awkward person; or a person wearing ragged and tattered clothes."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (a person, their body, etc.) to look awkward and stiff, like a scarecrow (noun sense 1).\n\nTo splay (one's arms) away from the body, like the arms of a scarecrow.","To splay (one's arms) away from the body, like the arms of a scarecrow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scarecrow"},{"term":"frown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wrinkling of the forehead with the eyebrows brought together, typically indicating displeasure, severity, or concentration.","A downturn of the corners of the mouth, typically expressing sadness."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a frown on one's face.","To manifest displeasure or disapprobation; to look with disfavour or threateningly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scarecrow","blocks":[{"text":"A scarecrow is a decoy or mannequin that is often in the shape of a human. Scarecrows are usually dressed in old clothes and placed in open fields to discourage birds from disturbing and feeding on recently cast seed and growing crops. Scarecrows are used around the world by farmers, and are a notable symbol of farms and the countryside in popular culture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Kakashi2.jpg/330px-Kakashi2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scarecrow"},{"title":"Frown","blocks":[{"text":"A frown is a facial expression in which the eyebrows are brought together, and the forehead is wrinkled, usually indicating displeasure, sadness or worry, or less often confusion or concentration.\nThe appearance of a frown varies by culture. An alternative usage in North America is thought of as an expression of the mouth. In those cases when used iconically, as with an emoticon, it is entirely presented by the curve of the lips forming a down-open curve. The mouth expression is also commonly referred to in the colloquial English phrase, especially in the United States, to \"turn that frown upside down\" which indicates changing from sad to happy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Bildnis_eines_unbekannten_Mannes.jpg/330px-Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Bildnis_eines_unbekannten_Mannes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/%E5%AE%89%E5%85%A8%E5%B8%BD%E3%82%92%E8%A2%AB%E3%81%A3%E3%81%9F%E6%A1%88%E5%B1%B1%E5%AD%906180154.jpg/500px-%E5%AE%89%E5%85%A8%E5%B8%BD%E3%82%92%E8%A2%AB%E3%81%A3%E3%81%9F%E6%A1%88%E5%B1%B1%E5%AD%906180154.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/%E5%AE%89%E5%85%A8%E5%B8%BD%E3%82%92%E8%A2%AB%E3%81%A3%E3%81%9F%E6%A1%88%E5%B1%B1%E5%AD%906180154.jpg/500px-%E5%AE%89%E5%85%A8%E5%B8%BD%E3%82%92%E8%A2%AB%E3%81%A3%E3%81%9F%E6%A1%88%E5%B1%B1%E5%AD%906180154.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A scarecrow wearing a helmet (Japan)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E5%AE%89%E5%85%A8%E5%B8%BD%E3%82%92%E8%A2%AB%E3%81%A3%E3%81%9F%E6%A1%88%E5%B1%B1%E5%AD%906180154.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Circle_of_scarecrow_children_at_Joe%27s_Scarecrow_Village.JPG/500px